    "description_md": "Cetacean (whale, dolphin, porpoise) sightings and on-effort visual line-transect survey segments from quarterly CalCOFI cruises, 2004-2022 (effort through 2021). Curated by the Scripps Whale Acoustics Lab (Hildebrand / Baumann-Pickering) and staged from the CalCOFI marine mammal Shiny app repository (CalCOFI/marmam-app). The same cruises also carry the Farallon Institute's seabird and marine mammal survey (farallon_bird-mammal), run by an independent observer team: both datasets are kept, so a cetacean group seen by both teams appears once in each, and summing the two counts the same animals twice. The behaviour codes (primary and other behaviour) are held back: they are bare numeric codes with no codebook yet (Q03), so no behaviour rows are published until the lab supplies one; they remain in the archived source.\n",
